tyle=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(199.18 100.936) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-90\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(180 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(269.951542 143.704) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-90\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(338.323083 147.9808) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" d=\"M 2912 0 L 2400 0 L 2400 877 L 243 877 L 243 1350 L 2112 4467 L 2912 4467 L 2912 1325 L 3558 1325 L 3558 877 L 2912 877 L 2912 0 z\nM 2368 4051 L 749 1325 L 2400 1325 L 2400 4051 L 2368 4051 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p94e2c36914\"><rect x=\"35.8\" y=\"10.472\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · From headcount to real capacity gained","note":null},"answer":"<p>Read literally, 55% faster across 2,000 developers sounds like 1,100 extra developers of capacity. But it only applies to coding time.</p> <p>Realistic: 2,000 × 40% coding × 25% less time × 70% using it = <b>140 developers' worth</b> of time, about $21M a year.</p> <p>Cost: 2,000 × $480 = $0.96M a year plus $0.5M once. <b>Worth roughly 22× its cost.</b></p>"},{"q":"Can the bank cancel the 150 planned hires?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Not all of them: the realistic gain is about 140 developers' worth, and it is spread across 2,000 people in small slices, not 140 free people.</p> <p>A prudent plan: hire about 80 instead of 150 (bank half the gain), and use the rest to clear the backlog. Review after six months of measured data.</p>"},{"q":"What could go wrong?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Quality:</b> AI-written code can contain bugs or security flaws; keep code review and automated security scanning</li> <li><b>Data:</b> make sure code and customer data don't leave the bank's control</li> <li><b>Measuring:</b> track delivery speed and defect rates, not just how often the tool is used</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Buy the assistant for all developers: it costs about $1.0M a year and is realistically worth about $21M of developer time (140 developers' worth), about 22× its cost. But the vendor's 55% applies only to coding, which is 40% of a developer's time, and not everyone uses the tool. So trim next year's hiring modestly, to about 80 rather than 150, and use the rest to clear the backlog. Keep code review and security scanning in place. Next step: measure delivery speed and defects for six months.","great":["Breaks the vendor's claim into time share × speed-up × adoption","Compares value with cost","Is cautious about turning time saved into fewer hires","Raises quality, security and measurement"],"id":77,"slug":"larchwood-bank"}